## Features by Phase

### projects `[MVP]`
- Catalog at `/app` with two clearly labelled groups: **Council projects** (from `GET /projects`, the only projects with an official score) listed first, then **Reference assessments** (curated, compiled from public sources; never presented as council reports). Search and category live in the URL (`?search=`, `?category=`) via `hooks/use-catalog-filters.ts`: search writes are debounced and use history `replace`, category chips are `aria-pressed` toggles. References page 24 at a time with "Show more"; empty filter results offer "Clear filters"; a council list failure shows an inline retry without hiding references.
- Council project report (`/app/projects/:slug`) order: status badge → official score with meaning ("higher is safer") and provenance ("Published by the governor council · Round N") → council findings (lifecycle explanation until a report is published; a separate link when a reference assessment exists) → market context (explicitly not part of the score) → discussion; side column shows review progress (`ProjectLifecycleSteps`, `aria-current="step"`) and the on-chain record. No simulated governor controls. Unknown slugs stop retrying on 4xx and show "Project not found".
- Reference assessment (`/app/reference/:slug`): "Reference assessment" notice, "Reference index" with meaning and disclaimer, analyst notes (not "governor council notes"), and a "Request a council review" link. No trading-venue promotion.
- Curated market-reference assets inspired by widely tracked CoinMarketCap listings.
- Local coin logos in `public/icons/{slug}.png` (synced from CoinGecko via `pnpm --filter web icons:sync`); `ProjectIcon` loads by slug with initials fallback.
- Lifecycle status badges (`lib/format.ts`): `in_analysis` → "In analysis", `ready` → "Awaiting governor review", `voting` → "Governor review", `closed` → "Report pending", `analyzed` → "Report published". Legacy API state names stay internal.
- Price movement panel on reference project detail (7-day chart, 24h/7d change; React Query refreshes on the same 12-hour interval as the API cache). A manual refresh stays disabled until that window ends. While a saved snapshot is refreshing, the panel keeps the price on screen and shows “Refreshing saved prices” instead of the first-load skeleton.
- Protocol fundamentals panel on project detail (TVL trend, fees/revenue, exploit history; hidden when unavailable e.g. pure L1 networks).
- Community submission form. `[Phase 2]`

### market `[MVP]`
- `ProjectPricePanel` on curated reference detail pages (24h, 7d, 1m, 1y change badges).
- `TopRatedProjectCard` on the landing hero (description, tags, price, 24h/7d/1m/1y changes, compact sparkline).
- SVG sparkline chart (`PriceChart`) with 1D/1W/1M/1Y range filters, hover crosshair, and green/red tone from period direction.
- `useMarketPrice` calls `GET /market/projects/:slug` and paints immediately from that slug’s compact `localStorage` snapshot (price, changes, 48 chart points, one entry per reference asset). Catalog cards show the saved price on reload before the card is fetched again. A fresh snapshot is not requested again until 12 hours have passed, and the Refresh control stays disabled until `expiresAt`. A refresh in flight keeps the saved price and shows “Refreshing saved price” instead of the loading skeleton. A failed refresh keeps showing the saved snapshot for 7 days (`stale: true`). The error state appears only when there is no snapshot from that week. CoinGecko is a direct fallback when the API itself cannot be reached.
- `MarketCacheWarmup` starts `market-cache.worker` on the first shell render. The worker fetches the reference catalog a few assets at a time and the page writes each snapshot into that slug’s local cache and into the open price query, so cards fill in as each asset arrives. A progress bar lists how many are saved and which assets are still loading, and hides once every tradable asset is saved. In dev, a toast appears at that point.

### protocol-metrics `[MVP]`
- `ProtocolMetricsPanel` on reference and live project detail pages below the price panel. TVL, fees, and revenue charts paint from a compact `localStorage` snapshot (one entry per slug, up to 48 assets) and refresh every 12 hours. Fee and revenue history keep two years so the valuation can score one-year growth; charts still offer 1W/1M/3M/1Y ranges. Network market cap feeds price-to-sales. Governance diversification and the security score are shown for protocols. Refresh stays disabled until the 12-hour window ends; a refresh in flight keeps the saved charts and shows “Refreshing saved data” instead of the first-load skeleton. A failed refresh keeps that snapshot for 7 days; the error appears only when nothing from that week is saved. The same snapshot feeds the landing and catalog hover summaries.
- Dev server proxies `GET /protocol-metrics/*` to the API (`vite.config.ts`); without this, the browser receives SPA HTML and metrics fail silently.
- **Protocol** projects: full panel (TVL, fees/revenue/DEX volume charts with **1W/1M/3M/1Y** ranges, chain + token bar breakdowns, **on-chain valuation model**, security incidents).
- **On-chain valuation:** always surfaced via `ProtocolValuationSection` — shows computed metrics when DeFi Llama fee/revenue data exists, or an explanatory empty state (stablecoin, missing fees, missing revenue). Bitcoin uses a reserve composite (`CW-Reserve-v1`) titled **Reserve valuation** (security budget, dilution, settlement). Fee/TVL and revenue/TVL remain visible and are labelled as not part of that score. Other chains keep **Network fee valuation**.
- **Stablecoin** projects (USDC, USDT): circulating supply, supply history, and supply-by-chain bar chart.
- **Chain** projects (L1/L2): TVL plus network-wide DEX volume, fees paid, and revenue captured (validator/protocol share of fees — not a dapp P&L). Charts use **1W/1M/3M/1Y** ranges when DeFi Llama indexes the series.
- Resolver tries protocol first for DeFi/infrastructure; L1/L2 slugs use chain TVL first, then protocol fallback.

### blog `[MVP]`
- Public blog at `/blog` with markdown-sourced articles (launch story, progress updates, roadmap).
- Content in `modules/blog/content/*.md`; metadata in `lib/posts.ts`; rendered via internal markdown parser in `lib/render-markdown.tsx`.
- Featured post on index, shared `ResourceLayout` navigation ("Blog" landmark, mobile sheet), "More from the blog" related articles and launch CTAs on article pages.
- Copy describes shipped capability only: evidence is shared in project comments and review requests are free during launch. `[MVP]`

### docs `[MVP]`
- `/docs`, `/docs/whitepaper`, `/docs/tokenomics`, `/docs/governance`, `/docs/faq` inside `ResourceLayout`: sticky glass sidebar ("Documentation" landmark, `aria-current`) on desktop, a "Documentation menu" sheet below `lg`, opaque reading column, previous/next pager and an "On this page" list on `xl`.
- `DocsSection` derives a stable anchor id from its title (`lib/section-id.ts`) with a "Link to …" anchor; deep links such as `/docs/faq#reviews-scores` scroll after lazy content loads.
- `DocsTable` renders a labelled, keyboard-focusable scroll region so wide tables never overflow the page.
- Governance and tokenomics docs open with a pre-launch callout (CWT not minted, no mint date; figures are the planned design), and the FAQ says CWT cannot be bought. Governance docs state that in-app voting and delegation are not available yet (votes and `delegate` are wallet transactions); tokenomics marks review fees as planned. `[MVP]`

### comments `[MVP]`
- Public comment thread (read by all, post when authenticated). Guests get a "Sign in to comment" link that returns to the project; a failed post keeps the draft and shows an inline alert. Comments inform the council but never change the score.
- No per-comment fee: the API stores `comment_fee_paid` but charges nothing, so the UI makes no fee or transaction claims. TODO(docs): reinstate fee copy only if an anti-spam fee flow ships.

### auth `[MVP]`
- Email/password registration and login with session cookies after OTP verification, inside a glass auth panel (`AuthShell`) with a value column on desktop. Errors are inline (`FormAlert`, `role="alert"`) and distinguish incorrect credentials, invalid/expired codes or links, rate limiting, server errors and network failures (`lib/auth-error-message.ts`).
- Return destination: sign-in/sign-up links carry `?next=` (`hooks/use-auth-links.ts`); `lib/return-to.ts` accepts only in-app paths (rejects absolute, protocol-relative, backslash and `/auth/*` targets). The pending email, OTP purpose and destination live in `sessionStorage` (`lib/pending-verification.ts`) so the code page survives a reload. `GuestRoute` honours a safe `next` for signed-in visitors.
- OTP page title mirrors the email heading for its purpose (verify email vs sign in) and states the 10-minute expiry; resend has a 30-second client cooldown and invalidates earlier codes.
- Forgot-password and reset-password flow (token-based, single use, 30-minute expiry; enumeration-safe confirmation; dev surfaces the link until email infra ships). Successful reset returns to `/auth/signin?reset=1`.
- Three-step onboarding (how scores work, how to take part, optional wallet address) with progress, Back and Skip; finishes at the preserved destination. Linking an address needs no signature; wallet sign-in from the account menu explains that signing sends no transaction and reports rejected signatures.
- Public-key (wallet) linking for CWT protocol governance votes (not project score voting).
- Wallet connect via RainbowKit lives inside the logged-in profile dropdown (not the top nav).

### analysis `[MVP]`
- **In analysis** tab on the Projects page (`/app?view=in-analysis`; `/app/in-analysis` and `/analysis` redirect there). The tab badge counts open requests plus council projects in analysis. Panel: status legend that separates request status from published reviews ("A request is not a review"); request cards (`article`) with readable status (`lib/request-status.ts`: `pending`/`paid` → Received, `in_review` → Under review, `approved` → Accepted, `rejected` → Declined), next step, submitted date and council notes; load error with retry; council projects in analysis. Team/admin see triage buttons (Start review, Accept, Decline) that PATCH only the status — no generated verdict notes.
- **Analysis Request** page (`/app/analysis-request`): free during launch (API `feeAmount` is always `0`; no payment flow). Guests get sign-in / sign-up links that return to the form. Grouped form with inline validation mirroring the API schema (name 1–200, http(s) URL, description 10–5000), focus on the first invalid field, single submission while pending, data kept on failure with error-specific messages (session expired → sign in again, 429, 5xx, network). Success shows a persistent, focused "Request received" panel with a queue link; "Your requests" lists `GET /analysis-requests/me`.

### profile `[MVP]`
- Unified profile page (`/app/profile`, also `/app/me`): identity header (role badge "Governor council" for admin, "Platform team" for team), settings form with inline validation matching `PATCH /users/me` limits (nickname 2–32, display name ≤120, X ≤64, bio ≤1000, public wallet address format), PFP upload (Web Worker compresses to a base64 data URI before save), in-place "Profile saved." confirmation and a failure alert that keeps edits (session-expired link on 401). Side column: wallet status, council tools (team/admin only: review queue, manage projects) and the "Your requests" history. Guests get a sign-in prompt that returns to the profile. `[MVP]`

### scoring `[MVP]`
- `ScorePanel` ("Official safety score") shows the governor-published score, its meaning and round provenance, or "No official score yet".
- **Credit-style ratings:** each safety score maps to paired **S&P** and **Moody's** letter grades (`AAA`/`Aaa` … `D`) and a top-level group — **Investment grade** (`AAA`–`BBB`) or **Speculative grade** (`BB`–`D`). See `lib/ratings/credit-rating.ts`.
- Enriched external-signal display. `[Phase 3]`

### governance — launch requirement
- View **protocol** proposals, cast CWT governance votes, see results (Governor + token). `[MVP]`
- Pre-launch status (current): hero states "CWT not minted" with no mint date, a milestone tracker (contracts built and tested → proposal UI built → deployment, mint and distribution not scheduled → voting after mint → delegation `[Phase 2]`), who decides today (council, core team, community), what CWT will govern, an honest empty proposals state and a token FAQ ("Can I buy CWT today?"). Update `governance/lib/governance-milestones.ts` when a milestone ships. `[MVP]`
  - List: readable states (Not open yet, Voting open, Passed, Not passed, Executed) with a state legend, retry on error and an honest empty state.
  - Detail: lifecycle steps, description, proposer, voting window and a "Your vote" panel. Voting calls `castVote(proposalId, support)` on the Governor via wagmi when `VITE_GOVERNOR_ADDRESS` is set; otherwise the panel explains that in-app voting isn't enabled. Panel states: disconnected (connect wallet), wrong network (switch chain), checking, read failure, ineligible (no voting power at `proposalSnapshot`), already voted, ready, awaiting wallet confirmation, pending, confirmed (explorer link), cancelled by the user and failed (with the contract's reason). Wallet code is lazy-loaded with the panel.
- Community proposal creation UI. `[Phase 1]`
- Vote delegation UX (`ERC20Votes`). `[Phase 2]`
- Full DAO/treasury dashboards. `[Final]`

### reputation `[MVP → Phase 1]`
- Show reviewer credentials for governor council members. `[MVP]` `/app/u/:address` validates the address client-side, shows council status neutrally for non-members ("Not on the governor council"), shows reviewer weight only for members and states that only council members publish official scores.
- Detailed multi-factor reviewer accountability profile. `[Phase 1]`

### rewards `[Phase 1]`
- Display reviewer compensation and misconduct penalty history.

### notifications `[Phase 1]`
