### Platform & UX
- Uber-inspired light theme (cream/yellow/black), Raleway font, fully rounded Shadcn components; blueprint grid background on all pages. `[MVP]`
- Global shell: skip link → glass header (Projects, Governance, Resources menu — the review queue is a tab inside Projects | ⌘K search + theme toggle + auth/account menu) → focusable `main#main-content` (focus moves there on client navigation) → footer with Product/Resources/Account groups and a request CTA. Below `lg`, a centered floating glass pill keeps Home, Projects and Governance in a row with Menu. A single foreground pill slides behind the selected tab. Only that tab shows its label; scrolling hides that label too. A tap shows it again so the next tap navigates or opens the sheet (resources, account actions and theme). All links come from `components/layout/navigation.ts`. `[MVP]`
- Scrollbars stay hidden in every browser (`scrollbar-width: none`, zero-size `::-webkit-scrollbar`). The bar is not `display: none`, so Logitech and Rapoo wheel drivers still scroll the page and nested regions. `[MVP]`
- Liquid-glass design language (see `docs/redesign/DESIGN.md`): `--glass-*` tokens with `.glass-nav`, `.glass-card`, `.glass-card-flat` and `.glass-panel` surfaces; alpha tuned for WCAG AA text contrast; opaque fallback under `prefers-reduced-transparency` and when `backdrop-filter` is unsupported; at most three blurred layers on screen. Semantic `info`, `chart-1..5` and `*-strong` status text tokens. Landing palette `--tone-{amber,coral,violet,sky,teal,pink}` (+ `-strong` AA text variants) used via `ToneIcon` (`components/ui/tone-icon.tsx`) for resource/menu/methodology tiles and section eyebrows. Framer Motion honors `prefers-reduced-motion` via `MotionConfig`. `[MVP]`
- Landing review lifecycle uses one bordered card with a five-stage selector, a two-column detail panel on desktop, compact numbered selectors and stacked details on mobile, and previous/next controls. Only the selected stage receives a sky accent; stages do not accumulate rainbow fills. The tour is opt-in and manual navigation pauses it. `[MVP]`
- Landing motion uses glass easing and 160/240/320 ms chrome transitions, with short staggered reveals. The hero sonar center is a counter-rotating reticle with expanding blooms, not a sample report card. Reduced motion shows final content immediately, stops decorative loops, and keeps lifecycle selection manual (the opt-in 4-second tour runs only while visible). The reference tape is the same passing row on phones and desktops. Grade bars use a contained horizontal scrollport with 44px targets. `[MVP]`
- All shell routes and the footer reserve bottom-pill clearance plus the device safe area below `lg`. Page hero actions stack on phones; docs/blog sheets remain within the available width. `[MVP]`
- Command palette search (debounced, race-conditioned) over council projects (listed first, tagged "Council") and reference assessments (tagged "Reference"). Below `lg` it opens beneath the header. The header and mobile tab bar stay above the overlay. `[MVP]`
- Toasts via Sonner, icons via Remix Icon, forms via React Hook Form. `[MVP]`
- Error reporting via Sentry. `[MVP]`
- Embeddable score widgets/badges. `[Phase 3]`
- PWA / mobile experience. `[Phase 3]`

## Functional Requirements (by feature & phase)

### projects `[MVP]`
- R1: Browse and search council projects and reference assessments without connecting a wallet; filters are shareable URLs.
- R2: View a council project report with lifecycle status, official score provenance and market context; view reference assessments labelled as such.
- R3: Team UI to create/update/transition projects. `[MVP]` (role-gated `[Phase 2]`)
